    <summary>Breaks a large Outlook mailbox file into several new PSTs using a size threshold, a year, month or week period, top-level folders or senders. A simple way to split PST file data offline.</summary>
    <description>This package installs Split PST File Software, a desktop program that can split PST file archives into several smaller Outlook data files while Outlook itself stays closed. Admins reach for it when a user's email store has outgrown its quota or hurts Outlook performance, since splitting by a rule yields new PSTs and the source .pst or .ost is opened read-only.

![Split PST File screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/spl/spl-v4-folders.png)

## How to use Split PST File Software

1. Open the program, browse to a .pst or .ost file on disk and load it.
2. Tick the folders for the run in the tree. Subfolders are included automatically.
3. Optionally narrow the message list with the Subject, From, To or Body filter.
4. Choose the split rule: size threshold, date period, top-level folder or sender.
5. Keep the Deleted Items and Junk exclusion and the CSV report on, pick an output location and press Start.

Trial note: an unregistered copy processes part of the messages, chosen as a sample, and then shows a reminder window. Registering removes this limit, and each part then holds the complete set of its messages.

![Split PST File screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/spl/spl-v4-date.png)

## Four ways to split PST mail

- By Size fills each part up to the threshold you enter, 1 GB if you leave the default, and no message is ever cut in two.
- By Date writes one PST per year, month or week. Items without a date go to an undated part.
- By Folder turns each top-level folder of the mailbox into its own file.
- By Sender groups mail by the normalized sender address, and addresses with only a few messages share others.pst.

Whichever method you use to split PST file content, the output gets names like part_1.pst, 2024.pst or 2024-01.pst, and the folder structure is rebuilt inside each part. A CSV report in UTF-8 lists every part with its file name, item count and size, which helps when you check a pst split later.

![Split PST File screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/spl/spl-v4-done.png)

## Who it is for

IT staff preparing mailboxes for an Outlook import export job or a move to new hardware, where a large outlook pst file is awkward to copy. Consultants who must split PST file into smaller parts before archiving old years on separate media. Users who see splitting as a way to lower the risk of corruption, since an ANSI outlook data file is capped at 2 GB and a Unicode one at 50 GB. This PST splitter runs the whole job locally, so no mail is uploaded.

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of a commercial program. Full use requires a license (lifetime, 1-year, monthly plan or business), which removes the sample limit. Plans and the feature list are on the [split PST file](https://www.softorbits.net/split-pst/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) page.

## FAQ

### How to split PST file archives from Outlook?

Load the archive in the program, choose one of the four rules and press Start. Outlook can stay closed, and the new parts appear in your destination folder.

### What software can split PST files?

A dedicated pst splitter like this one, which reads Outlook data files directly on Windows 10 and 11. It writes regular PST files that you can attach in Outlook later.

### Can I split a PST file into one archive per year?

Yes, use By Date with the Year preset. Each year of mail becomes its own PST, and the Month or Week presets give smaller slices when a year is still too large.
